                %strong 7
                (2005) 203 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0409024"} arXiv:hep-th/0409024
                %em
                  ,
                  = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1367-2630/7/1/203"} doi:10.1088/1367-2630/7/1/203
            %li
              %p
                Dmitri V. Fursaev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Black Hole Thermodynamics and Perturbative Quantum Gravity
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Quantum+Gravity"} Handbook of Quantum Gravity
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.06081"} arXiv:2210.06081
          %p
            Review from the point of view of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} thermal field theory
          %ul
            %li#FullingRuijsenaars87
              S.A. Fulling, S.N.M. Ruijsenaars,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Temperature, periodicity and horizons
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www1.maths.leeds.ac.uk/~siru/papers/p26.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(87)90136-0"} doi:10.1016/0370-1573(87)90136-0
          %p
            Review in the context of presence of a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
          %ul
            %li
              Robert B. Mann:
              %em Black Hole Chemistry: the first 15 years
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.01830"}> arXiv:2508.01830
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Basic introductory accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Wald"}> Robert Wald
                ,
                %em The Thermodynamics of Black Holes
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9912119"}> arXiv:gr-qc/9912119
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Bekenstein"}> Jacob Bekenstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "http://www.scholarpedia.org/article/Bekenstein-Hawking_entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
                %strong 3
                10 (2008) 7375
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
                \:
                %em Introduction to Black Hole Thermodynamics
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.16795"}> arXiv:2412.16795
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and further review:
          %ul
            %li
              S. P. de Alwis,
              %em Comments on Entropy Calculations in Gravitational Systems
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2304.07885"}> arXiv:2304.07885
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            A more general discussion which identifies thermodynamic properties of all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horizons"} horizons
            appearing on gravity (not just
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole"} black hole
            horizons) was given in
          %ul
            %li#Jacobson95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ted+Jacobson"}> Ted Jacobson
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Thermodynamics of Spacetime: The Einstein Equation of State
              %strong 75
              (1995) 1260-1263 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/9504004"}> arXiv:gr-qc/9504004
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.1260"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevLett.75.1260
          %p
            This article showed that under some assumptions the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein+equations"} Einstein equations
            can even be
            %em derived
            from identifying gravitational horizon area with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropy"} entropy
            and them imposing laws of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermodynamics"} thermodynamics
          %p For more comments and more references on this observation see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thanu+Padmanabhan"}> Thanu Padmanabhan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Thermodynamical Aspects of Gravity: New insights
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.5004"} arXiv:0911.5004
          %p
            (Later authors tried to argue that derivations like this show that gravity is not a fundamental force of nature such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            or the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+nuclear+force"} strong nuclear force
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/entropic+force"} entropic force
            that arises only from more fundamental forces in a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermodynamic+limit"} thermodynamic limit
          %p
            Discussion of black hole entropy from entropy of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+field+theory"} conformal field theory
            associated with the horizon has been given in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Carlip"}> Steve Carlip
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Entropy from Conformal Field Theory at Killing Horizons
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://xxx.lanl.gov/abs/gr-qc/9906126"} arXiv:gr-qc/9906126
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Carlip"}> Steve Carlip
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Horizon Constraints and Black Hole Entropy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0408123"} arXiv:hep-th/0408123
          %p and reviewed in
          %ul
            %li#Carlip05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Carlip"}> Steve Carlip
                ,
                %em Horizon constraints and black hole entropy
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0508071"}> arXiv:gr-qc/0508071
                )
            %li#Carlip07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Carlip"}> Steve Carlip
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Symmetries, Horizons, and Black Hole Entropy
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0705.3024"} arXiv:0705.3024
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ashoke+Sen"}> Ashoke Sen
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Logarithmic Corrections to Schwarzschild and Other Non-extremal Black Hole Entropy in Different Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:1205.0971"} arXiv:arXiv:1205.0971
            %li
              %p
                Aitor Lewkowycz,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"} Juan Maldacena
                %em Generalized gravitational entropy
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1304.4926"}> arXiv:1304.4926
                )
            %li
              %p
                Aidan M. McSharry, Harvey S. Reall:
                %em On the third law of black hole mechanics for supersymmetric black holes
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2507.06870"}> arXiv:2507.06870
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p A discussion of the “black hole firewall problem”:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ahmed+Almheiri"}> Ahmed Almheiri
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Marolf"} Donald Marolf
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joseph+Polchinski"} Joseph Polchinski
              = succeed "," do
                %em Black holes: complementarity or firewalls?
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:1207.3123"} arXiv:1207.3123
          %p
            On black hole entropy in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mirjam+Cvetic"}> Mirjam Cvetic
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Malcolm+J.+Perry"} Malcolm J. Perry
              %em Quantization of Black Hole Entropy for Black Holes in Subtracted Geometry
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.14247"}> arXiv:2504.14247
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#via_wickrotated_thermal_field_theory Via Wick-rotated thermal field theory
          %p
            Discussion via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wick+rotation"} Wick rotation
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+field+theory"} Euclidean field theory
            on spacetimes with compact/periodic Euclidean time (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/thermal+field+theory"} thermal field theory
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curved+spacetimes"} curved spacetimes
          %ul
            %li#FullingRuijsenaars87
              %p
                S.A. Fulling, S.N.M. Ruijsenaars,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Temperature, periodicity and horizons
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www1.maths.leeds.ac.uk/~siru/papers/p26.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0370-1573(87)90136-0"} doi:10.1016/0370-1573(87)90136-0
            %li#GibbonsPerry78
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gary+Gibbons"}> Gary Gibbons
                , Malcolm J. Perry,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Black Holes and Thermal Green Functions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/79482"} jstor:79482
          %h3#interpretation_in_string_theory Interpretation in string theory
          %p
            Microscopic explanation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bekenstein-Hawking+entropy"} Bekenstein-Hawking entropy
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+holes+in+string+theory"} black holes in string theory
            as
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+states+of+D-branes"} bound states of D-branes
          %ul
            %li#StromingerVafa96
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"}> Andrew Strominger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cumrun+Vafa"} Cumrun Vafa
              = succeed "," do
                %em Microscopic Origin of the Bekenstein-Hawking Entropy
              = succeed ")" do
