                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.22775"}> arXiv:2509.22775
                  ]
            %p reviewed in:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hao+Geng"}> Hao Geng
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Recent Progress in Quantum Gravity: Karch-Randall Braneworld, Entanglement Islands and Graviton Mass
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "http://hdl.handle.net/1773/49427"} hdl:1773/49427
            %p and discussion of what to do about this problem:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hao+Geng"}> Hao Geng
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Karch"} Andreas Karch
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Carlos+Perez-Pardavila"} Carlos Perez-Pardavila
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Suvrat+Raju"} Suvrat Raju
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lisa+Randall"} Lisa Randall
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcos+Riojas"} Marcos Riojas
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sanjit+Shashi"} Sanjit Shashi
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Information Transfer with a Gravitating Bath
                %strong 10
                103 (2021) [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2012.04671"}> arXiv:2012.04671
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://scipost.org/10.21468/SciPostPhys.10.5.103"} doi:10.21468/SciPostPhys.10.5.103
            %p
              Claim that the whole argument relies on the false assumption that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/split+property"} split property
              holds for
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+gravity"} quantum gravity
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Suvrat+Raju"}> Suvrat Raju
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Failure of the split property in gravity and the information paradox
                %strong 39
                064002 [
                %a{:href => "https://iopscience.iop.org/article/10.1088/1361-6382/ac482b"}> doi:10.1088/1361-6382/ac482b
                ,
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.05470"} arXiv:2110.05470
            %p Review in:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nirmalya+Kajuri"}> Nirmalya Kajuri
                  ,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %a{:href => "https://science.thewire.in/the-sciences/unitarity-entanglement-islands-holography-information/"} Of Islands, Holograms and Saving Quantum Physics From a Black Hole Paradox
                %blockquote
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi …
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\ldots]
                    a few sceptics have argued that while the calculations are correct, they don’t help resolve the black hole information-loss paradox. The troubles stem from the reservoir attached to the anti-de Sitter universe. The physicists who authored the island papers assumed that gravity stopped at the boundary of the anti-de Sitter space and didn’t enter the reservoir. This is not an innocuous assumption. […] The key takeaway is that the island way to recover information and save unitarity works perfectly well – if you slightly modify Einstein’s theory of gravity. These criticisms have been around for some two years now, and physicists are yet to resolve them in print. […] physicists continue to publish papers by the hundreds about the entanglement islands but few attempt to answer whether the islands are compatible with the Einsteinian gravity of our universe. […]
            %p
              Claim of reconciliation of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/causal+locality"} causal locality
              in the island proposal, under the explicit assumption of massive gravity:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hao+Geng"}> Hao Geng
                \:
                %em The Mechanism behind the Information Encoding for Islands
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.08703"}> arXiv:2502.08703
                ]
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  Anna Karlsson,
                  %em Concerns about the replica wormhole derivation of the island conjecture
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2101.05879"}> arXiv:2101.05879
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  Harvendra Singh:
                  %em Islands and Icebergs contribute nothing to the Page curve (System with a symmetrical bath)
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2210.13970"}> arXiv:2210.13970
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  Saskia Demulder, Alessandra Gnecchi, Ioannis Lavdas,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dieter+L%C3%BCst"} Dieter Lüst
                  %em Islands and Light Gravitons in type IIB String Theory
                  [
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2204.03669"}> arXiv:2204.03669
                  ]
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Martinec"}> Emil Martinec
                  \: “Thus far, picturesque evocations of quantum wormholes remain largely just that – picturesque evocations.” (
                  %a{:href => "https://www.math.columbia.edu/~woit/wordpress/?p=13113#comment-241963"}> 2nd Nov 2022
                  )
            %p
              Argument that discussion of the issue in the toy example of 2d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/JT+gravity"} JT gravity
              does not actually generalize to higher dimensions:
            %ul
              %li#LandgrenShekar24
                Filip Landgren, Arvind Shekar,
                %em
                  Islands and entanglement entropy in
                  = succeed "-dimensional" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.01653"}> arXiv:2401.01653
                ]
            %p Debate between a proponent and a critic :
            %ul
              %li#PeningtonRaju24
                %em>
                  Islands and Black Hole Information ft.
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Suvrat+Raju"} Suvrat Raju
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geoff+Penington"} Geoff Penington
                , podcast at
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/@theoreticallypodcasting7390"} Theoretically Podcasting
                (9 Mar 2024) [
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/ZCIho8geEfI"}> YT
                ]
            %p See also:
            %ul
              %li
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Samir+Mathur"}> Samir Mathur
                , podcast comment (2024) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://x.com/Hassaan_PHY/status/1789623310348698044"}> x:1789623310348698044
                ]
            %p Reaction to the criticism:
            %ul
              %li
                Stefano Antonini, Chang-Han Chen, Henry Maxfield,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geoff+Penington"} Geoff Penington
                %em An apologia for islands
                [
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.04311"}> arXiv:2506.04311
                ]
          %h3#relation_to_weight_systems_on_chord_diagrams Relation to weight systems on chord diagrams
          %p
            An argument that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT+duality"} dual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/black+hole+thermodynamics"} black hole thermodynamics
            are generically given by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/single+trace+operators"} single trace operators
            that evaluate to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems"} weight systems
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chord+diagrams"} chord diagrams
            (such as observables on
            = succeed "-like" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SYK+model"} SYK model
          %p
            (for more see at
            = succeed "):" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weight+systems+on+chord+diagrams+in+physics"} weight systems on chord diagrams in physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Micha+Berkooz"}> Micha Berkooz
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Prithvi+Narayan"} Prithvi Narayan
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joan+Sim%C3%B3n"} Joan Simón
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chord diagrams, exact correlators in spin glasses and black hole bulk reconstruction
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1806.04380"} arxiv:1806.04380
